    </tbody>
   <caption unique="1012590">Instruction Operand Encoding</caption>
   </table>
  </operand_table>
 <longdesc><para unique="1012592">The XTEST instruction queries the transactional execution status. If the instruction executes inside a transaction&#173;ally executing RTM region or a transactionally executing HLE region, then the ZF flag is cleared, else it is set.</para>
  </longdesc>
 <operation>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1012594">XTEST</title>
   <programlisting>IF (RTM_ACTIVE = 1 OR HLE_ACTIVE = 1)
	THEN
		ZF := 0
	ELSE
		ZF := 1
FI;</programlisting>
   </section>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1012602">Flags Affected</title>
   <programlisting>The ZF flag is cleared if the instruction is executed transactionally; otherwise it is set to 1. The CF, OF, SF, PF, and AF, flags are cleared.</programlisting>
   </section>
  </operation>
 <subsection title="Intel C/C++ Compiler Intrinsic Equivalent">
  <programlisting>XTEST int _xtest( void );</programlisting>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="SIMD Floating-Point Exceptions">
  <para unique="1012607">None.</para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Other Exceptions">
  <variablelist>
   <variablelistentry>
    <term>#UD</term>
    <listitem><para unique="1012609">If CPUID.07H.00H:EBX.HLE[4] = 0 and CPUID.07H.00H:EBX.RTM[11] = 0.</para>
     </listitem>
    <listitem><para unique="1012610">If LOCK prefix is used.</para>
     </listitem>
    </variablelistentry>
   </variablelist>
  </subsection>
 </instruction>
